@title Every construct
@start intro
@import chapters/*.squiffy
@ui story.js
    squiffy.set("score", 0);

@ui
    squiffy.registerHelper("shout", (text) => text.toUpperCase());
<div class="banner">Welcome</div>
---

[[intro]]:
@set score = 10
@set name = Bob
@set greeting := Hello, {{name}}!
@set best = @score
@set coins *= 2
@set has_key
@set not visited
@unset has_key
@inc score 5
@dec health
    console.log("Started");
    if (squiffy.get("score") > 5) { squiffy.set("lucky", true); }
# A heading

You wake up. This is **bold**, *italic* and `code`. <span class="note" title="{{name}}">HTML</span>

    Indented text after the first line of text isn't JavaScript.

Go to the [[kitchen]], [[look around]](garden), or [[carry on>]].
Try [the door](door, tried=1), [the window], or [[next]](>, score+=1).
Read [the manual](https://example.com/manual). ![A cat](cat.png)

{{score}} points, {{get "player name"}} and {{{raw_html}}}.
{{#if score > 100 and (seen "door")}}
Well done.
{{else if not has_key}}
No key.
{{else}}
{{random (array "red" "green") set="colour"}}
{{/if}}
{{set "gold" gold + price * 2}} costs {{= price - discount}}, {{inc "my-count" -1}}
{{#animate "typewriter" interval=30}}Typing...{{/animate}}
{{! a comment }}
{{!-- a longer comment --}}
{{embed "intro"}} {{embed "greeting"}}
<!-- an HTML comment -->

[door]:
@clear
    squiffy.set("door_opened", true);
The door opens.

[[kitchen]]:
@end
It's a kitchen.

